# What a source distribution carries.
#
# This file changes almost nothing: setuptools' defaults already produced a
# correct sdist, verified by building one and running its tests. It exists so
# that what ships is **declared** rather than whatever the build backend
# happened to decide -- which is the same argument this package makes about
# every other undeclared fact, applied to itself.
#
# The documents are included because README.md points at them by relative path.
# An sdist that carries the pointer and not the target is a broken reference in
# the one file everybody opens first.
include kinemata.toml
include AIPOLICY.md
include CHANGELOG.md
graft docs
graft examples

# Never ship: other projects' material, kept in this tree as test corpora and
# examples only, and all of it gitignored. Named here as well because gitignore
# and sdist contents are two different mechanisms, and relying on one to enforce
# the other is exactly the coupling this package reports elsewhere.
prune corpus
prune canon-files
exclude keyspace-manifest.yaml
exclude clause-traceability-*.md
exclude settings-keyspace-*.md
exclude system-design-*.md

# Build and test residue.
prune .github
global-exclude *.py[cod] __pycache__ .DS_Store
